nk":{"fieldSizeRank":19,"finishersRank":14,"finishRateRank":62,"winningTimeRank":13,"winningTimeRankDir":9,"totalRaces":98},"recordContext":{"womenWouldHaveWonMen":{"mostRecentYear":1974,"mensWinner":"Derek PREISS","mensTime":"06:02:49"}},"narrative":"The 2005 Comrades Marathon was the 80th running of the race, run in the 'down' direction from Pietermaritzburg to Durban over 89.170 km. The race was held on Thursday, 16 June. Conditions: Cold at start. Fine and mild later. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nSipho NGOMANE claimed the men's title in 05:27:11, ahead of Oleg KHARITONOV (05:29:16) and Andrew KELEHE (05:31:45). Tatyana ZHIRKOVA won the women's race in 05:58:51, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:10:40).\n\nTatyana ZHIRKOVA's 05:58:51 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1974 (Derek PREISS, 06:02:49).\n\nFrom a field of 13,892 entries, 11,728 runners crossed the finish line (84.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 9,727 men and 2,001 women (17.1% female). The average finish time was 10:00:57.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 637 Silver, 2,425 Bill Rowan, 5,712 Bronze, 2,934 Vic Clapham. 2,349 runners (20.0%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Schalk GROBLER in 11:59:58.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 50% of the finishers, with 5,818 seniors (avg 09:45:15) and 5,910 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}